AoLS are more in the category of, "If you don't want to use it, don't use 
it." The game already tracks how many times your life has been saved; that 
in itself gives the impetus for more skilled players to minimize its use 
("You survived after having been killed 12 times" will start feeling a 
little cheesy after a while.) The game is more likely to give you AoR before 
AoLS anyway (through Sokoban), and once someone begins finding out how 
useful reflection is, the allure of lifesaving diminishes.

IOW, the game already gives plenty of reasons not to overuse AoLS. Why 
eliminate something that skilled players recognize as of limited value 
anyway? It's a boon to less-skilled players. Leave it in.

